## Cursor-Specific Guidelines

### Memory System Usage

- Use memory tools to track project context and user preferences
- Update memories when user provides feedback or corrections
- Reference memories when making decisions about code style or approach

### Git Integration

- Always run `git status` (or use `gst` alias) before commits
- Ask for verification before updating progress and committing
- Ensure pre-commit hooks pass before finalizing commits

### Code Organization Awareness

- Follow existing code organization patterns
- Alert user when refactoring is needed for current or future tasks
- Maintain consistency with established module structure

### Task Verification Protocol

- Check if each new task is required before proceeding
- Present both recommendation (proceed/not) and plan
- Confirm with user before deleting obsolete tests
- Ensure all tests use pytest command (not `python -m pytest`)
